
    SIGLISTER v 0.2      30 January 1994
    
1.  SIGLISTR is a utility program for Starnet and MEBBSNet sysops which
    will create msglistX.txt and msglistX.gr1 files.  Those files are
    read and displayed by the BBS program when callers enter message
    areas.  The msglist files are created in a two column format.
    
    SIGLISTR also creates msglist0.txt and msglist0.gr1 files which may
    be useful for sysops who do not divide their message areas into
    Special Interest Groups (SIGs).
    
2.  SIGLISTR may be run from the Workbench, by clicking on the icon, or
    it may be run from the shell, by entering the filename.  SIGLISTR and
    its associated configuration file, siglistr.config, are written to
    operate only from the BBS root directory.
    
3.  The file 'siglistr.config' contains two lines of text.  The first is
    the name of the file which siglistr should examine to find the names
    and SIG numbers of the BBS message areas.  The default filename is
    starnet.con
    but you may change it.  That is why there is a configuration file.
    The second line is the path to the msglistX.XXX files.  The default
    path is starnet:txt/
    And, as usual, the pathname _must_ end in a colon ':' if the output
    files go to a device, or _must_ end in a slash '/' if the output
    files go to a directory. 
    Lines beginning with a semicolon ';' in the configuration file
    are ignored by the program.  Use such for comments.
    
4.  Files included in this archive are:
    SIGLISTR the executable program
    SIGLISTR.info the program's icon
    siglistr.config the sample configuration file
    siglistr.doc which is this text file
    
5.  Siglistr is copyright 1994 by Robert Davis.  However, I do not
    need or want payment for the program.  If you find it useful,
    I would appreciate a note either on paper or via email.
    As always, the usual disclaimers apply.  This program is warranted
    to take up storage space on your disk drive.  If you have problems
    using it, let me know, but I am not responsible for any damage
    or difficulties caused by your use of the siglistr program.
    
6.  As this is an early version of siglistr, I expect it will not be 
    perfect.  And there may be room for improvement.  Configurable 
    colours are certainly possible.  You are asked to send comments
    to the author of the program ... that's me.
    
